{"parentUuid": "5c5bcc7b-1fc0-4c64-92e6-7f1936533ef5", "isSidechain": true, "promptId": "89daae11-03b7-48a9-8a56-4740cd2ec122", "agentId": "a1c0594bdb2077365", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_017tCFN8vUkezztQsmvEaVtD", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t<!DOCTYPE html>\n2\t<html lang=\"en\">\n3\t<head>\n4\t  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n5\t  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n6\t  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"AI-powered study platform grounded in learning science\">\n7\t  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#B86E3A\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\">\n8\t  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1A1A18\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\">\n9\t  <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n10\t  <meta name=\"apple-mobi...[truncated]"}]}, "uuid": "2d83385d-5776-4be2-bbaa-e6f442d8ec9e", "timestamp": "2026-04-25T20:30:53.556Z", "sourceToolAssistantUUID": "5c5bcc7b-1fc0-4c64-92e6-7f1936533ef5", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/test/Projects/studyengine", "sessionId": "3f5802ab-0587-4c78-8a7e-80ca419e724f", "version": "2.1.117", "gitBranch": "test-branch", "slug": "hazy-honking-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid": "2d83385d-5776-4be2-bbaa-e6f442d8ec9e", "isSidechain": true, "agentId": "a1c0594bdb2077365", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "id": "msg_0146YGQTFWU8mhZ7xGes4p3o", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I have all the file contents. WebFetch was denied, so I'll apply the standard Web Interface Guidelines rules from my training knowledge to conduct the audit. Let me now produce the full checklist-style report.\n\n---\n\n## Web Interface Guidelines Audit\n\n**Files audited:**\n- `app/templates/quiz/loading.html`\n- `app/templates/units/partials/extraction_status.html`\n- `app/routes/jobs.py` (backend context)\n- `app/templates/base.html` (base context, first 80 lines)\n\n---\n\n### Accessibility\n\n#### `quiz/loading.html`\n\n**`loading.html:6` \u2014 FAIL: Polling container has no `aria-live` region**\nThe `#quiz-seed-poll` div is swapped via HTMX every 3 seconds. Screen readers will not announce status changes unless the container (or an ancestor) has `role=\"status\"` or `aria-live=\"polite\"`. A user who is blind will have no idea the page is doing anything.\n\n**`loading.html:4` \u2014 PASS: Status text is present**\n\"Generating your first questions\u2026\" and the 15\u201330 second expectation are meaningful and informative.\n\n**`loading.html` \u2014 FAIL: No `role=\"status\"` or `aria-live` on the outer wrapper**\nThe outer `<div>` also lacks a landmark role. This is a full-page loading state and should be wrapped in `<main id=\"main-content\">` or at minimum have `role=\"main\"`. (The base template's `{% block content %}` does not supply a `<main>` element per the first 80 lines.)\n\n#### `units/partials/extraction_status.html`\n\n**`extraction_status.html:1\u20138` \u2014 FAIL: Polling div has no `aria-live` or `role=\"status\"`**\nSame issue as above. The div swaps itself every 2 seconds; status changes are invisible to assistive technology.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:11` \u2014 FAIL: `onclick=\"location.reload()\"` link is not accessible**\nThe \"refresh to see them\" anchor has `href=\"\"` (empty, causes page jump to top on some browsers) and uses `onclick` to reload. A screen reader will read this as a link but the behavior is non-obvious. Use `href=\"javascript:void(0)\"` or `<button>` if the intent is a reload action, and add an `aria-label` describing the action (e.g., `aria-label=\"Reload page to see extracted topics\"`).\n\n**`extraction_status.html:14` \u2014 PASS: Error state is visible and has meaningful text**\n\"Topic extraction failed. Try re-uploading the PDF.\" is clear and actionable.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:14` \u2014 FAIL: Error state not announced to screen readers**\nThe `failed` branch renders a plain `<div>` with no `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live=\"assertive\"`. An error that appears after polling should announce itself. This is the most important accessibility failure in the file.\n\n---\n\n### Semantic HTML\n\n**`loading.html:3` \u2014 FAIL: No `<main>` landmark**\nThe block content is a bare `<div>`. Base template does not inject `<main id=\"main-content\">` (the skip link in `base.html:31` targets `#main-content` but there is no corresponding element in `base.html` or in this template). The skip link is broken.\n\n**`loading.html:4` \u2014 WARN: `<p>` used for a heading-level status message**\n\"Generating your first questions\u2026\" reads semantically like an `<h1>` or `<h2>` for this page state but is a `<p>`. For a full-page loading screen this is a minor issue, but using a heading would give the page a proper document outline.\n\n**`extraction_status.html` \u2014 PASS: `<div>` is appropriate for an inline status fragment**\nThis is a partial injected into a larger page, so a `<div>` container is fine. No heading needed.\n\n**`jobs.py:115` \u2014 FAIL: Script-tag redirect instead of HX-Redirect header**\n```python\nreturn HTMLResponse(\n    f'<script>window.location=\"/courses/{slug}/quiz/{quiz_id}/question/1\";</script>'\n)\n```\nThe seed-status-redirect endpoint injects a `<script>` tag to navigate when the job is ready. The correct HTMX pattern is to return `HX-Redirect` (or `HX-Location`) as a response header, which HTMX handles natively without injecting JavaScript. The current approach:\n- Breaks if the user has JavaScript errors elsewhere\n- Is semantically wrong (HTMX is already loaded and handles this)\n- Does not stop polling \u2014 the script fires but the hx-trigger on the replaced element may continue if the swap misbehaves\n\nThe correct fix:\n```python\nfrom starlette.responses import Response\nresponse = Response(status_code=200)\nresponse.headers[\"HX-Redirect\"] = f\"/courses/{slug}/quiz/{quiz_id}/question/1\"\nreturn response\n```\n\n---\n\n### HTMX Patterns\n\n**`loading.html:6\u201311` + `jobs.py:122\u2013128` \u2014 PASS: Polling stops on completion via outerHTML swap**\nWhen status is `ready`, the server returns a `<script>` redirect (see above \u2014 wrong mechanism, but polling does stop). When status is `failed`, it returns a static `<p>` with no `hx-trigger`, so polling stops. The `hx-swap=\"outerHTML\"` pattern correctly replaces the polling element.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:1\u20138` \u2014 PASS: Polling stops on terminal states**\nWhen `status == \"done\"` or `status == \"failed\"`, the template renders a plain `<div>` with no `hx-trigger`, so polling halts. The `hx-swap=\"outerHTML\"` correctly removes the polling element from the DOM.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:1` \u2014 WARN: No timeout guard for infinite polling**\nIf the backend job gets stuck in `pending` or `running` permanently (worker crash, DB corruption), the page will poll forever. There is no client-side timeout or max-retry limit. Consider adding a `hx-trigger=\"every 2s [window.__extractionAttempts < 60]\"` guard, or a server-side staleness check.\n\n**`jobs.py:104\u2013128` \u2014 FAIL: `seed-status-redirect` uses script-tag navigation (see above)**\nThis is both a semantic HTML and HTMX pattern failure. Replace with `HX-Redirect` header.\n\n**`jobs.py` \u2014 PASS: Course scoping is correct**\n`get_course_for_user` is used in all endpoints. Unit ownership is checked (`unit.course_id != course.id`). No authorization bypasses found.\n\n---\n\n### Mobile / Responsive\n\n**`loading.html:3` \u2014 PASS: `max-width:480px` with `margin:auto` is mobile-appropriate**\nThe container will not overflow on small screens. `padding:var(--space-6)` provides adequate side guttering.\n\n**`loading.html:4\u20135` \u2014 PASS: Font sizes are adequate**\n18px for the primary message and 14px for supporting text are readable on mobile.\n\n**`loading.html:10` \u2014 PASS: 13px tertiary text is marginal but acceptable**\n\"Waiting for worker\u2026\" at 13px is at the low end. Not a failure but worth watching.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:6` \u2014 PASS: Inline status fragment is small and text-only**\nNo touch targets to evaluate; this is informational text only.\n\n**`extraction_status.html:11` \u2014 FAIL: \"refresh to see them\" link has no minimum touch target**\nInline anchor text inside a 13px `<div>` with `padding:var(--space-2) 0` will have a touch target well below the 44\u00d744px WCAG guideline. If this is tappable on mobile, it needs more padding.\n\n---\n\n### Focus Management\n\n**`loading.html` \u2014 FAIL: Focus is not managed after HTMX swap**\nWhen HTMX replaces `#quiz-seed-poll` with the error state or redirect script, focus remains wherever it was (typically body or the replaced element, which is now gone). For the error case specifically, focus should move to the error message so keyboard/screen reader users are aware of the change. Use `hx-on::after-swap` or `htmx:afterSwap` event to call `focus()` on the newly injected error element.\n\n**`extraction_status.html` \u2014 FAIL: Same focus management gap on error/done states**\nWhen polling resolves to `done` or `failed`, no focus shift occurs.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| # | File | Issue | Severity |\n|---|------|-------|----------|\n| 1 | `loading.html:6` | No `aria-live`/`role=\"status\"` on polling container | High |\n| 2 | `loading.html:3` | No `<main>` landmark; skip link target `#main-content` is missing | High |\n| 3 | `extraction_status.html:1` | No `aria-live` on polling div | High |\n| 4 | `extraction_status.html:14` | Error state not `role=\"alert\"` \u2014 not announced to screen readers | High |\n| 5 | `jobs.py:115` | Script-tag redirect instead of `HX-Redirect` header | High |\n| 6 | `extraction_status.html:11` | `href=\"\"` reload link \u2014 broken semantics, inaccessible label | Medium |\n| 7 | `extraction_status.html:11` | Touch target too small for mobile | Medium |\n| 8 | `loading.html` | No focus management after HTMX swap to error state | Medium |\n| 9 | `extraction_status.html` | No focus management after swap to done/failed states | Medium |\n| 10 | `extraction_status.html:1` | No timeout guard \u2014 infinite polling if job stalls | Low |\n| 11 | `loading.html:4` | Status heading is a `<p>` not an `<h1>`/`<h2>` | Low |\n\n---\n\n### Top 3 Fixes to Prioritize\n\n**1. Add `role=\"status\"` and `aria-live=\"polite\"` to both polling containers** \u2014 one attribute each, zero risk, immediate screen reader benefit.\n\n**2. Replace script-tag redirect with `HX-Redirect` header in `jobs.py:114\u2013116`** \u2014 correct HTMX pattern, more robust, avoids injecting JavaScript into HTMX swap targets.\n\n**3. Add `role=\"alert\"` to error states** \u2014 `extraction_status.html` line 14 and the failed branch in `jobs.py:118\u2013121` both need this so errors are announced without focus shift."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_creation_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_read_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "output_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_crea